---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import River from '../components/River.astro';

const gh = 'https://github.com/agentux-os';
const docs = `${gh}/agentux/blob/main/docs`;
const adr = (n: string) => `${gh}/agentux/blob/main/docs/adr/${n}`;
---
<Base
  title="AgentUX: the Linux distribution for coding agents"
  description="AgentUX is a Linux distribution where every coding agent works as one team: Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and Antigravity CLI behind one cockpit, talking over an agent bus, from issue to reviewed pull request."
  path="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-copy">
      <h1>The Linux distribution where every coding agent works as one team.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        AgentUX ships Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and Antigravity CLI already installed and wired together on an
        immutable Fedora base: one cockpit over all of them, an agent bus so they can talk to each other, and an
        orchestrator that takes an issue to a reviewed pull request.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/download/">Download</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/download/#live">Try the live ISO</a>
      </div>
      <p class="status">
        Pre-release. Fedora Kinoite 44 with bootc, signed images, x86_64 and aarch64.
        <a href="#status">What is tested so far</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap hero-art">
      <River />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="what" aria-labelledby="what-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="what-h">Bring every agent you already pay for</h2>
        <p>
          Running agents in parallel worktrees is solved. Getting agents from different vendors to work on the same task,
          and keeping track of them, is not. AgentUX does that part, and leaves inference with the providers: your own logins
          and API keys, no GPU required.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="pillars">
        <div>
          <dt>One interface for every vendor</dt>
          <dd>
            Sessions, diffs and permission requests from any harness look the same in the cockpit, and land in one approvals
            inbox. The vendor's own TUI is always one key away.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Agents that talk to each other</dt>
          <dd>
            An implementer can ask a reviewer from another vendor to check its diff, hand off a task, or escalate a decision to
            you, through a mediated bus where every message is logged.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>From issue to reviewed pull request</dt>
          <dd>
            The pipeline (plan, implement, test, review, open the PR) is declared in <code>agentux.yaml</code> and versioned
            with your repository. You are asked only for the decisions that are yours.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>A system agents cannot break</dt>
          <dd>
            An immutable, image-based OS with one-step rollback. Every task runs in its own git worktree, and gate checks can
            run in rootless Podman.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="screenshots" aria-labelledby="shots-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="shots-h">What it looks like</h2>
        <p>Captured by CI from the real images booted in QEMU. The runs on screen use fake agents, so nothing is billed.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="shot shot-main">
        <img
          src="/screenshots/cockpit-plan-approval.png"
          width="1920"
          height="1080"
          alt="The AgentUX cockpit on the live ISO: a run board with two demo runs, one of them waiting for plan approval in the inbox on the right."
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>The cockpit: a run board for every project, and an inbox for what is waiting for you.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="shot-row">
        <figure class="shot">
          <img
            src="/screenshots/boot-animation.gif"
            width="450"
            height="300"
            alt="The boot splash: the AgentUX penguin swimming in place, its wake streaming back, with a wavy progress line."
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>The boot splash. The penguin swims while the system starts.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot">
          <img
            src="/screenshots/installer.png"
            width="1920"
            height="1080"
            alt="The AgentUX web installer on the live ISO."
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>The installer on the live ISO, in AgentUX colours.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot">
          <img
            src="/screenshots/first-boot.png"
            width="1920"
            height="1080"
            alt="First-boot setup over the AgentUX wallpaper."
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>First boot: create your account, then the agent CLIs install themselves.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="how-h">How a run works</h2>
        <p>Hand AgentUX an issue or a prompt, from the cockpit or the <code>aux</code> CLI. This is what happens next.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="how">
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>AgentUX creates a git worktree and a branch for the task.</li>
          <li>A planner writes a plan, and waits for your approval if the pipeline asks for it.</li>
          <li>An implementer harness works in the worktree. Its session streams to the cockpit.</li>
          <li>Tests and linters gate the result. Failures loop back to the implementer, up to a limit.</li>
          <li>A reviewer from a different vendor reviews the diff, and talks to the implementer over the agent bus when it needs to.</li>
          <li>AgentUX opens the pull request.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="yaml">
          <p class="yaml-cap"><code>agentux.yaml</code>, the default pipeline, shortened</p>
          <pre><code>roles:
  planner:     {'{'} harness: claude-code {'}'}
  implementer: {'{'} harness: claude-code {'}'}
  reviewer:    {'{'} harness: codex {'}'}   <span class="c"># another vendor</span>

pipeline:
  - step: plan
    approve: true            <span class="c"># wait for you</span>
  - step: implement
  - step: gate
    checks: [lint, test]
    on_fail: implement
    max_attempts: 3
  - step: review
    on_changes_requested: implement
  - step: pull_request</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="layers">
        <h3 class="layers-h">The parts</h3>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Harnesses over ACP</dt>
            <dd>
              Each provider's own CLI, driven through the <a href="https://agentclientprotocol.com">Agent Client Protocol</a>,
              with headless modes as the fallback. AgentUX never handles your credentials.
              <a href={adr('0002-harness-integration-via-acp.md')}>ADR 0002</a>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>The agent bus</dt>
            <dd>
              <code>agentuxd</code> exposes the bus to every harness as an MCP server: <code>post_message</code>,
              <code>request_review</code>, <code>handoff</code>, <code>get_run_state</code>, <code>ask_human</code>. The daemon routes
              every message and caps turns per exchange, so two agents cannot loop forever.
              <a href={adr('0004-unified-interface-and-agent-bus.md')}>ADR 0004</a>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>The orchestrator</dt>
            <dd>
              A workflow engine in <code>agentuxd</code> runs the pipeline as a persisted state machine, with budgets per run and
              approvals where you ask for them. <a href={adr('0003-workflow-engine.md')}>ADR 0003</a>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>The cockpit and <code>aux</code></dt>
            <dd>
              A Tauri desktop app over every session the daemon runs, and its terminal twin, which works over SSH. Any session can
              switch to its vendor's TUI on the same conversation.
              <a href={adr('0007-terminal-mode-is-a-session-handoff.md')}>ADR 0007</a>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>The OS</dt>
            <dd>
              Fedora Kinoite 44 built with bootc: KDE Plasma, or a Hyprland tiling session in the second image. Immutable, with
              atomic updates and rollback, and every image signed with cosign.
              <a href={adr('0010-image-variants-and-system-identity.md')}>ADR 0010</a>
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="status-h">Where it stands</h2>
        <p>
          AgentUX is pre-release (agentux-core 0.4.2 and agentux-desktop 0.4.5). Runs already go from prompt to pull request
          through real harness sessions. This is what has been checked, and what has not.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="status-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Verified in CI</h3>
          <ul class="checks yes">
            <li>Both variants build and pass a first-login smoke test on amd64 and arm64.</li>
            <li>The Plasma image boots nightly under QEMU/KVM on x86_64 and takes a fake-agent run to a pull request.</li>
            <li>The x86_64 live and installer ISOs are installed in a VM before they are published.</li>
            <li>Image signatures are checked against the policy installed systems enforce.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Not verified yet</h3>
          <ul class="checks no">
            <li>Full cross-vendor runs with real Claude Code, Codex and Antigravity sessions. OpenCode has been tried.</li>
            <li>Booting the arm64 image on real hardware or a VM: CI's arm64 runners have no KVM.</li>
            <li>Booting the Hyprland image. Its configuration is checked, not run.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="status-more">
        The <a href={`${gh}/agentux#roadmap`}>roadmap</a> lists what is done and what comes next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="docs" aria-labelledby="docs-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="docs-h">Documentation</h2>
        <p>The docs live with the code, on GitHub.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="doc-links">
        <li>
          <a href={`${docs}/getting-started.md`}>Getting started</a>
          <span>From install to a first run that ends in a pull request: first login, the cockpit tour, <code>aux</code>.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${docs}/getting-started.md#5-agentuxyaml`}>agentux.yaml</a>
          <span>Roles, checks, the pipeline, bus limits, budgets and container isolation.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${gh}/agentux-os#install`}>Installing and updating</a>
          <span>ISOs, <code>bootc switch</code>, release channels, rollback and verifying signatures.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${gh}/agentux/tree/main/docs/adr`}>Design decisions</a>
          <span>Every architectural decision, recorded as an ADR.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${gh}/agentux-core`}>agentux-core</a>
          <span>The <code>agentuxd</code> daemon, the <code>aux</code> CLI, the workflow engine and the harness adapters.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${gh}/agentux-desktop`}>agentux-desktop</a>
          <span>The cockpit app and the Plasma configuration.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${gh}/agentux/tree/main/brand`}>Brand</a>
          <span>The swimming penguin, the wordmark and the colours.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section closing" aria-labelledby="closing-h">
    <div class="wrap closing-row">
      <h2 id="closing-h">Boot it, look around, install when you want to keep it.</h2>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/download/">Download</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/download/#bootc">Switch from Fedora Atomic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 3.3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-stretch: 87.5%;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    max-width: 19ch;
  }

  .lead {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    max-width: 40rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.6vw, 1.25rem);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .status {
    max-width: 30rem;
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .status a {
    margin-left: 0.35rem;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .hero-art {
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  /* On wide screens the penguin swims up beside the copy, and the lanes run in under it. */
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .hero-art {
      margin-top: -12.5rem;
    }

    .lead {
      max-width: 33rem;
    }
  }

  /* Pillars */
  .pillars {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0 clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pillars > div {
    padding-block: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .pillars dt {
    font-family: 'Martian Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-stretch: 87.5%;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .pillars dt::before {
    content: '';
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.5rem;
    height: 0.5rem;
    margin-right: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    vertical-align: 0.15em;
  }

  .pillars dd {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  /* Screenshots */
  .shot {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .shot img {
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--ink);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .shot figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .shot-row {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
  }

  .shot-row img {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .shot-row .shot:first-child img {
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  /* How it works */
  .how {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: 0.95rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .steps li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .steps li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    font-family: 'Martian Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .yaml-cap {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .layers {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .layers-h {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .layers dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(17rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 0 clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .layers dl > div {
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .layers dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .layers dd {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .layers dd a {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Status */
  .status-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .status-grid h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .checks {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .checks li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.8rem 0 0.8rem 1.9rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .checks li::before {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.8rem;
    font-family: 'Martian Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .checks.yes li::before {
    content: '\2713';
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .checks.no li::before {
    content: '\25CB';
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .status-more {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* Docs */
  .doc-links {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(19rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 0 clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .doc-links li {
    padding-block: 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .doc-links a {
    font-family: 'Martian Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-stretch: 87.5%;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .doc-links a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .doc-links span {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }

  /* Closing */
  .closing {
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .closing-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem 3rem;
  }

  .closing h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .closing .cta-row {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .pillars,
    .how,
    .status-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .shot-row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
